# V-27 — D-42 accepted. The trap is real. And **the 32 are one gap, not 32 findings.**

## The trap you refused: confirmed real, and worse than it looks

Re-pointing `c28()` at `build_run_assets` gives **0 violations**. The BLOCKING failure passes and
every unearned `lit` survives untouched. You were right that nobody proposed it and someone would
— it is the most natural-looking way to apply *your own ruling*, which is exactly what makes it
dangerous.

## Who they are — and the distribution is the finding

**All 32 are R0. All 32 are `CURRENT`. All 32 are Class A — no `build_run_assets` record of any
kind.** Class B (ran but never completed) is **empty**. None of them failed. None was observed to
run at all.

*(32 vs C-28's 31 is `bg_panchanga`, `asset_kind='service'`, dropped by the DATA-kind filter —
established at V-22.)*

## This is **one structural gap**, and the ratio settles it

| | with any `build_run_assets` record |
|---|---|
| R0 assets | **6 of 40** |
| non-R0 assets | **87 of 88** |

Per-asset flakiness would spread across layers. This is concentrated in **exactly the one layer
built by the other runner**. That is loophole **L-03 / defect D-19** verbatim: `global_runner.py`
builds L0 with no `build_runs` row and no cockpit visibility.

**The `lit` states are unearned *as measured by run records* because the runner that builds L0
does not write run records.**

## And they are not hollow — which changes the repair

`bg_muhurta_lattice` holds **164,886 rows** with no run record at all. These are **real data whose
provenance was never recorded**. "Unearned" here means *no witness to the build*, not *nothing was
built*. A rung gate that read them as empty would be as wrong as one that read them as earned.

## The consequence for R0, in terms nobody has used yet

**§8.3 item 2 — "state is earned … never asserted" — cannot be satisfied for 34 of R0's 40 assets
by any amount of measuring the data that is there.** There is no run record to inspect, and none
can be manufactured honestly (H6).

It requires those assets to be **rebuilt through a runner that records the run**. Which makes
**L-03/D-19's runner unification a precondition of R0's freeze, not a parallel workstream.**

Better to state that before R0 opens than to discover it at the gate.

